{"type":"message","id":"d8ef4151","parentId":"059120db","timestamp":"2026-04-17T20:12:06.809Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The shared pool progress management table (TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd) has records but they're empty. Let me check the supervision table for recent records and also check the task kanban for any tasks that might be stale (over 60 minutes without update).\n\nLet me now check the main task kanban (D8A9bsKpnaetWhsTp73cZfzcnoh - 龙虾调度总线) for tasks and check for stale tasks.\n\nAlso let me check if there's a newer task supervision table in the kanban. Let me look at the records in BMWPb0n1RapmFusxHe1c0mFmnab's \"任务执行记录\" table - it returned empty, so maybe the supervision records are in another table.\n\n\nNow I'm pulling the latest records from the shared pool progress management table and examining the DeerFlow progress kanban (OR2wboXxkaDzqLsBZH2c9YMnnUe) which was mentioned in the daily notes as the DeerFlow专项研究 realtime progress board, then cross-referencing everything with the daily memory to get a complete picture of current task statuses.\n\nLooking at the kanban board records, I can see the status breakdown: 54 total tasks with 3 done, 5 dead historically, 小八 at 1 blocked, 小柱 with 2 done, 小云 at 1 done, 全员 with 1 done, and Qclaw with 2 dead. The task types include one running task from the previous hour's check record (recvh4Be2cS7js from 18:11), which is now overdue given the current time of 20:11. Now I need to check if there are other running tasks beyond just that check record, since the kanban shows more done tasks than what was documented before.\n\nThe total count of 54 seems quite high compared to the individual task numbers I'm seeing. I'm also noticing there are two separate bitables mentioned—the shared pool progress management table (TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd) and the hotel AI native progress log (Kdc4biRCqalOogs2NCScAdKDnhf)—and I should clarify which one is the actual shared pool since the naming seems inconsistent with what the daily notes reference.\n\nI'm also seeing that the task supervision table (BMWPb0n1RapmFusxHe1c0mFmnab) has an empty task execution records table, so I need to pull from a different source to get the latest task statuses. The daily notes indicate a check record from 18:11 (recvh4Be2cS7js) was marked as done, and the current time is 20:11, which is exactly 2 hours old—but I don't see any 60-minute timeout being triggered in the recent entries, so I'm missing some context about what's actually aging out.\n\nLooking back at the daily notes, the 14:11 check marked a task as dead after 12 hours, and the 17:11 entry shows all tasks without new dead ones. Now I need to find the actual running tasks to understand what's currently active and potentially overdue.\n\nThe kanban board shows various tasks distributed across different handlers—小八 has one blocked task, 小柱 and 小云 each have two done tasks, 全员 has one done task, and Qclaw has two dead tasks. I should verify the exact task IDs and current statuses by examining the kanban table directly, then cross-reference with the DeerFlow专项研究看板 to confirm what's actually in progress versus what's been completed or failed."},{"type":"text","text":"Let me check the DeerFlow progress kanban and get more recent records from the shared pool:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0r4ogejk81r1_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"OR2wboXxkaDzqLsBZH2c9YMnnUe"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0r4ogejk81r1_2","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"TeIZbungWasADfsKcnjcogmMnCd","table_id":"tbl0HJYbY1tp3Nyi","page_size":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":177645670